{"parameters":{"model":"dxn:com.anthropic.model.claude-opus-5.default","stream":true,"tools":[{"name":"eval","description":"Runs code against the workspace and returns whatever that code printed. This is the only tool: every read, every write and every operation happens inside it.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"code":{"type":"string","description":"The program, in the dialect the system prompt describes. Print anything you need to see."}},"required":["code"],"additionalProperties":true}}]},"prompt":{"content":[{"options":{},"role":"system","content":"## Code mode\n\nYou have exactly one tool, `eval`, which runs the body of an async JavaScript function against\nthis workspace and returns whatever that code printed. Nothing else is visible to you: a value\nyou do not `print` never reaches you. Do not use `import` or `require` — the API below is\nin scope.\n\nPrefer one `eval` call that does the whole job — query, inspect, change, print — over a call\nper step. Print the specific values you need to reason about, not whole objects, and keep the\noutput small.\n\n### API\n\n- `print(...values)` — adds a line to this call's output. Strings go through verbatim,\n  everything else is printed as JSON.\n- `await query(typename, props?)` — objects of that typename, optionally narrowed by exact\n  property values, e.g. `await query('example.com/type/Task', { status: 'open' })`.\n- `await make(typename, props)` — a new object; it is not stored until you add it.\n- `await add(obj)` / `await remove(obj)` — store or delete an object.\n- `update(obj, (obj) => { obj.field = value; })` — the only way to change a stored object.\n- `await flush()` — waits for pending writes to land; call it before printing a final\n  confirmation.\n\n### Types\n\nEvery registered type and its fields. This is the whole schema — do not introspect it further.\n\n- `com.example.type.expando` — \n- `com.example.type.task` — title, status, priority\n- `org.dxos.type.feed` — name, kind, namespace, rewindFrom\n- `org.dxos.type.skill` — name, description, instructions, tools, agentCanEnable, mcpServers, hooks\n- `org.dxos.type.instructions` — name, description, input, output, text, skills, objects, commands\n- `org.dxos.type.function` — name, description, updated, source, inputSchema, outputSchema, services, binding, icon\n- `org.dxos.type.assistant.chat` — name, viewType, remote, feed, instructions, model, tasks\n- `org.dxos.type.trigger` — runnable, spec, enabled, remote, concurrency, inputNodeId, input\n- `org.dxos.type.tag` — label, hue\n- `org.dxos.type.alarm` — wakeAt, message, created\n- `org.dxos.type.view` — query, projection\n\n### Operations\n\nThe skills above describe their capabilities as tools; in code mode they are NOT tools. Each one\nis an async function on `ops`, taking one argument matching its parameter schema. A failed\noperation throws, so wrap a call you expect to fail in `try`/`catch`. The names are kebab-case,\nso they are indexed rather than dotted.\n\n- `await ops[\"com-example-operation-score\"](input)` — Scores a task title for urgency. Returns the title's length as the score.\n  input: {\"type\":\"object\",\"properties\":{\"title\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"The title to score\"}},\"required\":[\"title\"],\"additionalProperties\":true}\n\n## Skills Definitions\n\n<skill>\n  \n</skill>"},{"options":{},"role":"user","content":"Score every open task of type com.example.type.task and store each score on the task's priority field. Then tell me which task scored highest."},{"options":{},"role":"assistant","content":[{"options":{},"type":"text","text":"I'll query the open tasks, score each one, and store the results."},{"options":{},"type":"tool-call","id":"toolu_01FUfSEihqP7Z6VpaRVjiwRj","name":"eval","params":{"code":"const tasks = await query('com.example.type.task', { status: 'open' });\nprint('open tasks:', tasks.length);\nconst results = [];\nfor (const t of tasks) {\n  const r = await ops[\"com-example-operation-score\"]({ title: t.title });\n  print(t.title, '->', JSON.stringify(r));\n  results.push([t, r]);\n}\n"},"providerExecuted":false}]},{"options":{"anthropic":{"cacheControl":{"ttl":"5m","type":"ephemeral"}}},"role":"tool","content":[{"options":{},"type":"tool-result","id":"toolu_01FUfSEihqP7Z6VpaRVjiwRj","name":"eval","isFailure":false,"result":{"output":"open tasks: 2\nWrite the docs -> 14\nFix the build -> 13"},"providerExecuted":false}]}]},"response":[{"metadata":{},"type":"response-metadata","id":"msg_011CfAwhLJupr5G34FJWtqtJ","modelId":"claude-opus-5","timestamp":"1970-01-01T00:00:00.000Z"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-start","id":"0"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":"The"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":" score"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":" function returns the"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":" number directly, so I'll"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":" store that"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":" value on"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":" the pri"},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":"ority field."},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":"\n\n"},{"metadata":{"anthropic":{"info":{"type":"thinking","signature":""}}},"type":"reasoning-delta","id":"0","delta":""},{"metadata":{},"type":"reasoning-end","id":"0"},{"metadata":{},"type":"tool-params-start","id":"toolu_01BxqnqNEgc2Vdj2qjWHcGYq","name":"eval","providerExecuted":false},{"metadata":{},"type":"tool-params-delta","id":"toolu_01BxqnqNEgc2Vdj2qjWHcGYq","delta":"{\"code\""},{"metadata":{},"type":"tool-params-delta","id":"toolu_01BxqnqNEgc2Vdj2qjWHcGYq","delta":": \"cons"},{"metadata":{},"type":"tool-params-delta","id":"toolu_01BxqnqNEgc2Vdj2qjWHcGYq","delta":"t tasks"},{"metadata":{},"type":"tool-params-delta","id":"toolu_01BxqnqNEgc2Vdj2qjWHcGYq","delta":" = awai"},{"metadata":{},"ty